		},
		{
			"id":"8f2edaac0a42cb13",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Note: Some boards require scraping to retrieve job details\nThe expectation is that the AI agent has access to a browser. For Claude, this means using the claude-in-chrome extension. This can be a little tricky to get going - it is likely to report that it is installed but disabled. Some things to try when this happens:\n- restart the session\n- check via /mcp and /chrome\n- @browser can work, too\n\nFrom Claude:\n- **Persistence:** your config has \"Enabled by default\" on, so new sessions should connect on their own. If one doesn't, type `@browser` in the prompt.\n- **Job-search automation:** the `job-fetcher` agent for Jobgether and Indeed uses these tools. The allowlist in this project's `settings.local.json` covers `jobgether.com` and `www.indeed.com`, so those two sites are the ones it can use without prompting.\n- **Claude Desktop:** I didn't need to touch its native host manifest. If the connection drops later, quit Desktop, restart Chrome and use **Reconnect extension** in `/chrome`.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-490,
			"y":-1227,
			"width":500,
			"height":687
		},
